  tags: [spec, implemented]
- label: serve is the default command — running bare "pace" starts the server
  command: grep -q "serve" src/cli.ts
  tags: [spec, implemented]
- label: CLI startup reports malformed config as a config-prefixed error without a Bun stack trace
  command: tmp=$(mktemp); printf 'adapters:\n  - type: hackernews\npipelines:\n  - name: combined\n    sources: hackernews\n    transforms:\n      - type: latest\n        count: 10\nlayout:\n  direction: row\n  children:\n    - panel: combined\n      source: combined\n' > "$tmp"; out=$(timeout 3 env PORT=31409 bun run src/cli.ts serve --config "$tmp" 2>&1); status=$?; test "$status" -eq 1 && printf "%s" "$out" | grep -q "^config: pipelines\[0\]\.sources must be a list$" && ! printf "%s" "$out" | grep -q "Bun v\| at validatePipelineConfig\|pace listening"
  tags: [spec, bugbash, implemented]
- label: CLI startup reports configured adapter types missing from discovered runtime adapters as scheduler-prefixed errors before server startup
  command: tmp=$(mktemp); printf "adapters:\n  - type: definitely_missing_adapter\nlayout:\n  direction: row\n  children:\n    - panel: missing\n      source: definitely_missing_adapter\n" > "$tmp"; out=$(timeout 3 env PORT=31441 PACE_CONFIG="$tmp" bun run src/cli.ts serve 2>&1); status=$?; test "$status" -eq 1 && printf "%s" "$out" | grep -q "^scheduler: adapter type \"definitely_missing_adapter\" is configured but no matching adapter module was discovered$" && ! printf "%s" "$out" | grep -q "pace listening\|Bun v\| at startScheduler"
  tags: [spec, bugbash, implemented]
- label: the CLI launcher in src/cli.ts always chdir's to the directory containing its package.json (computed via const projectRoot = join(import.meta.dir, '..'); process.chdir(projectRoot)) before the dynamic import('./index'), ensuring tsconfig.json, node_modules resolution, default config paths and data/ dir are always from the project regardless of shell cwd or global bin invocation
