# runtime
- label: startScheduler in src/scheduler.ts prevents duplicate timer registration and overlapping jobs by early-returning if entries already exist, ensuring that even if invoked multiple times only one set of adapter/pipeline/prune timers exists (verified by double-start test reporting everyCount:1 instead of 2)
  command: cd /home/everlier/code/pace && bun run /tmp/sched-double-test.ts >/dev/null 2>&1 && cat /tmp/sched-double-evidence.json | grep -q '"everyCount": 1'
  tags: [bugbash-iter3, implemented]
- label: stopScheduler clears pending initial pipeline setTimeout timers (stored per PipelineEntry as initialTimer) in addition to interval timers, so that no runPipelineJob or new setInterval can fire after stopScheduler (verified by shutdown-timing test showing no extra logs post-delay, afterDelay count equals afterStop count)
  command: cd /home/everlier/code/pace && bun run /tmp/sched-shutdown-test.ts >/dev/null 2>&1 && cat /tmp/sched-shutdown-evidence.json | grep -q '"afterDelay": 2'
  tags: [bugbash-iter3, implemented]
- label: runAdapter/runPipelineJob log only short error strings (via errorMessage(err)) to console.warn and store lastError on their Entry; never dump full Error objects/stacks from periodic or refresh job failures (verified by error-path test capturing clean "error: Simulated..." without "Error: " prefix in logs/evidence)
  command: cd /home/everlier/code/pace && bun run /tmp/sched-error-test.ts >/dev/null 2>&1 && cat /tmp/sched-error-evidence.json | grep -q 'error: Simulated adapter network failure: ECONNRESET' && ! cat /tmp/sched-error-evidence.json | grep -q 'Error: Simulated'
  tags: [bugbash-iter3, implemented]
- scheduler.ts and cli.ts use the shared errorMessage(err: unknown) helper from adapters/types.ts (no local duplicate function definition in scheduler or inline String coercion in cli catch blocks); src/errorMessage.test.ts guards the helper with dedicated unit tests for Error, string/number/boolean, null/undefined, and plain objects (exact same behavior as before, now single source of truth across runtime and CLI layers) @timeboxed-iter3 @implemented
- scheduler.ts exported scheduler APIs and behaviors (startScheduler duplicate-start guard returning early without re-registering timers, missing adapter type errors prefixed "scheduler: adapter type ...", stopScheduler clearing all adapter/pipeline/prune timers including initial setTimeout, refreshSources selecting and running adapters+pipelines returning RefreshResult[] with status ok/skipped/failed; success paths log and persist via db) are guarded by dedicated unit tests in src/scheduler.test.ts (using hermetic temp DB via PACE_DB_PATH, mock adapters, console spies, before/afterEach cleanup with stop/close; exercising guard, errors, adapter fetch+save+no-transform path, refresh results, stop); behavior and error strings 100% preserved, 231+ tests remain green @timeboxed-iter42 @implemented

## refresh
- label: manual panel refresh surfaces adapter fetch failures with HTTP 502 instead of redirecting as success
  command: tmp=$(mktemp -d); repo="$tmp/repo"; rsync -a --exclude=.git --exclude=node_modules ./ "$repo/"; printf "import type { Adapter, AdapterConfig, ContentItem } from \"./types\";\n\nconst adapter: Adapter = {\n  name: \"bugbashfail\",\n  async fetch(_config: AdapterConfig): Promise<ContentItem[]> {\n    throw new Error(\"bugbash forced fetch failure\");\n  },\n};\n\nexport default adapter;\n" > "$repo/src/adapters/bugbashfail.ts"; printf "adapters:\n  - type: bugbashfail\n    refresh_interval: 60\nlayout:\n  direction: row\n  children:\n    - panel: failing\n      source: bugbashfail\n" > "$tmp/config.yaml"; port=31454; log="$tmp/server.log"; (cd "$repo" && env PORT=$port PACE_CONFIG="$tmp/config.yaml" bun run src/cli.ts serve > "$log" 2>&1) & pid=$!; cleanup() { kill "$pid" 2>/dev/null || true; wait "$pid" 2>/dev/null || true; rm -rf "$tmp"; }; trap cleanup EXIT; for i in $(seq 1 30); do curl -fsS "http://127.0.0.1:$port/health" >/dev/null 2>&1 && break; sleep 0.2; done; out=$(curl -i -sS -X POST "http://127.0.0.1:$port/refresh/failing"); printf "%s" "$out" | grep -q "^HTTP/1.1 502" && printf "%s" "$out" | grep -q "Refresh failed for bugbashfail" && ! printf "%s" "$out" | grep -q "Location: /"
  tags: [spec, bugbash, implemented]
- label: manual refresh of the all panel refreshes every configured adapter that contributes to the all source
  command: tmp=$(mktemp -d); repo="$tmp/repo"; rsync -a --exclude=.git --exclude=node_modules --exclude=data ./ "$repo/"; printf "import { existsSync, readFileSync, writeFileSync } from \"node:fs\";\nimport type { Adapter, AdapterConfig, ContentItem } from \"./types\";\n\nconst adapter: Adapter = {\n  name: \"bugbashcounter\",\n  async fetch(config: AdapterConfig): Promise<ContentItem[]> {\n    const counterPath = String(config.params?.counter_path ?? \"\");\n    const current = counterPath && existsSync(counterPath) ? Number(readFileSync(counterPath, \"utf-8\")) : 0;\n    const next = Number.isFinite(current) ? current + 1 : 1;\n    if (counterPath) writeFileSync(counterPath, String(next));\n    return [{ id: \"bugbashcounter-\" + next, title: \"Bugbash Counter \" + next, url: \"https://example.com/bugbashcounter/\" + next, source: \"bugbashcounter\", timestamp: new Date(), body: \"fetch \" + next }];\n  },\n};\n\nexport default adapter;\n" > "$repo/src/adapters/bugbashcounter.ts"; counter="$tmp/counter.txt"; printf "adapters:\n  - type: bugbashcounter\n    name: counter\n    refresh_interval: 60\n    params:\n      counter_path: \"$counter\"\nlayout:\n  direction: row\n  children:\n    - panel: all\n      source: all\n" > "$tmp/config.yaml"; port=$((32000 + $$ % 20000)); log="$tmp/server.log"; (cd "$repo" && env PORT=$port PACE_CONFIG="$tmp/config.yaml" bun run src/cli.ts serve > "$log" 2>&1) & pid=$!; cleanup() { kill "$pid" 2>/dev/null || true; wait "$pid" 2>/dev/null || true; rm -rf "$tmp"; }; trap cleanup EXIT; for i in $(seq 1 50); do curl -fsS "http://127.0.0.1:$port/health" >/dev/null 2>&1 && test -f "$counter" && break; sleep 0.2; done; before=$(cat "$counter"); out=$(curl -i -sS -X POST "http://127.0.0.1:$port/refresh/all"); sleep 0.5; after=$(cat "$counter"); printf "%s" "$out" | grep -q "^HTTP/1.1 303" && test "$after" -gt "$before"
  tags: [spec, bugbash, implemented]
- label: manual refresh requests for unknown panels return HTTP 404 instead of redirecting as success
  command: tmp=$(mktemp -d); printf "adapters: []\nlayout:\n  direction: row\n  children:\n    - panel: all\n      source: all\n" > "$tmp/config.yaml"; port=$((33000 + $$ % 20000)); log="$tmp/server.log"; env PORT=$port PACE_CONFIG="$tmp/config.yaml" bun run src/cli.ts serve > "$log" 2>&1 & pid=$!; cleanup() { kill "$pid" 2>/dev/null || true; wait "$pid" 2>/dev/null || true; rm -rf "$tmp"; }; trap cleanup EXIT; for i in $(seq 1 50); do curl -fsS "http://127.0.0.1:$port/health" >/dev/null 2>&1 && break; sleep 0.2; done; out=$(curl -i -sS -X POST "http://127.0.0.1:$port/refresh/not-a-panel"); printf "%s" "$out" | grep -q "^HTTP/1.1 404" && printf "%s" "$out" | grep -q "Unknown panel" && ! printf "%s" "$out" | grep -q "Location: /"
  tags: [spec, bugbash, implemented]
- label: manual refresh of a pipeline-backed panel refreshes the referenced pipeline source graph
  command: tmp=$(mktemp -d); repo="$tmp/repo"; rsync -a --exclude=.git --exclude=node_modules --exclude=data ./ "$repo/"; printf 'import { existsSync, readFileSync, writeFileSync } from "node:fs";\nimport type { Adapter, AdapterConfig, ContentItem } from "./types";\n\nconst adapter: Adapter = {\n  name: "bugbashcounter",\n  async fetch(config: AdapterConfig): Promise<ContentItem[]> {\n    const counterPath = String(config.params?.counter_path ?? "");\n    const current = counterPath && existsSync(counterPath) ? Number(readFileSync(counterPath, "utf-8")) : 0;\n    const next = Number.isFinite(current) ? current + 1 : 1;\n    if (counterPath) writeFileSync(counterPath, String(next));\n    return [{ id: "bugbashcounter-current", title: "Pipeline Counter " + next, url: "https://example.com/pipeline-counter", source: "bugbashcounter", timestamp: new Date(), body: "fetch " + next }];\n  },\n};\n\nexport default adapter;\n' > "$repo/src/adapters/bugbashcounter.ts"; counter="$tmp/counter.txt"; printf 'adapters:\n  - type: bugbashcounter\n    name: counter\n    refresh_interval: 60\n    params:\n      counter_path: "%s"\npipelines:\n  - name: combined\n    sources: [counter]\n    refresh_interval: 60\n    transforms:\n      - type: latest\n        count: 10\nlayout:\n  direction: row\n  children:\n    - panel: combined\n      source: combined\n' "$counter" > "$tmp/config.yaml"; port=$((35000 + $$ % 20000)); log="$tmp/server.log"; (cd "$repo" && env PORT=$port PACE_CONFIG="$tmp/config.yaml" bun run src/cli.ts serve > "$log" 2>&1) & pid=$!; cleanup() { kill "$pid" 2>/dev/null || true; wait "$pid" 2>/dev/null || true; rm -rf "$tmp"; }; trap cleanup EXIT; for i in $(seq 1 60); do curl -fsS "http://127.0.0.1:$port/health" >/dev/null 2>&1 && test -f "$counter" && break; sleep 0.2; done; sleep 5.5; before=$(cat "$counter"); out=$(curl -i -sS -X POST "http://127.0.0.1:$port/refresh/combined"); sleep 0.5; after=$(cat "$counter"); page=$(curl -sS "http://127.0.0.1:$port/"); printf "%s" "$out" | grep -q "^HTTP/1.1 303" && test "$after" -gt "$before" && printf "%s" "$page" | grep -q "Pipeline Counter $after"
  tags: [spec, bugbash, implemented]

