# bugbash
- label: the bugbash skill SKILL.md requires and documents that every invocation must create and use a unique fresh output directory (e.g. /tmp/bugbash-<target>-<YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS>/ following observed timestamped convention) rather than the static default /tmp/dogfood-output/ example, to prevent report.md and evidence collisions on concurrent runs or re-invocations
  command: grep -q 'unique fresh output directory' .agents/skills/bugbash/SKILL.md && grep -q 'timestamped' .agents/skills/bugbash/SKILL.md
  tags: [bugbash-iter4, implemented]
- label: the bugbash skill SKILL.md documents the agent/tool execution model for background and long-running processes (run_terminal_command with background:true param, kill_command_or_subagent by task_id, get_command_or_subagent_output) alongside or in place of raw shell '&' examples, and warns that literal '&' in command strings is rejected by the harness used in this project
